{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792710894,"nonce":"DuQulTbWKHK7q8nuPs8kKNEAMkk=","message":"Implemented in-process project windows and the shared desktop menu model, adopting Ashui window-local reactive/CSS/theme contexts and the shared platform/GPU manager. Existing projects open another workspace in a separate window; empty Welcome opens its selection in place. Native macOS menus follow the focused window; the shared model renders as an in-window Menubar on Windows/Linux. Window closure saves/discards/cancels per workspace. File/Folder project selection uses asynchronous macOS sheets, with selected project creation handed to the worker.\n\nValidation: Ashui native Windows.hx and menu regression suites pass. RayDE ProjectWindowChecks covers independent tabs/appearance, invalid project opening, save guard and discard, surviving original-window close, New Window after that close, worker native-selection handoff/cancellation and the eight-group in-window menu. Native AOT GUI checked New Window/Window menu/Close Window and survivors; the isolated native FileDialogWindow app checked sheet cancellation, reopening and selecting tests/fixtures/full/build.hxml. Windows/Linux platform execution is not available on this host; the shared in-window menu path was exercised on macOS.\n\nThe code-tab idle CPU regression was traced to unconditional theme updates in the Ashui refactor and fixed in 22a7462c180840d20adbb993fa9e28acae9e1c80. With 12 large tabs and Workbench.hx focused, native AOT interval CPU fell from 44.8–74.0% to 4.5–7.1%; unfocused idle was 0–0.1%. Frame traces show CSS flushes falling from about 30–35 ms to 0–0.1 ms; the focused caret fade still produces rendering work. The pin includes the fix.","files":null}]}